@startuml seq-delete-account
!theme plain
autonumber

actor "Creator" as U
participant "Web App\n(settings)" as C
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Identity Service" as IDN
database "Identity DB\n(PostgreSQL)" as IDB
queue "Kafka" as K
participant "Portfolio Service" as PF
participant "Site Publisher" as SP
participant "Media Service" as MS
database "Originals and public\nbuckets" as OBJ
participant "CDN" as CDN
participant "Analytics Aggregator" as AGG
database "ClickHouse" as CH

U -> C : "Delete my account"
C -> U : ask for the password (and a one-time code if MFA is on)
U -> C : confirm
C -> GW : POST /account/deletion {password, otp}
GW -> IDN : forward (accountId from JWT)
IDN -> IDN : verify password and second factor, rate limited
IDN -> IDB : BEGIN\nstatus = DELETION_REQUESTED\nrevoke all sessions\nerase email and password hash\nINSERT outbox (UserDeleted)\nCOMMIT
IDN --> GW : 202 Accepted
GW --> C : 202, "Your account is being deleted"

note over IDN
  Revoking the sessions logs the user out
  on every device. Access tokens expire
  within 15 minutes at the latest.
end note

IDN ->> K : UserDeleted {accountId}
K ->> PF : UserDeleted
PF -> PF : unpublish every portfolio, delete the profile
PF ->> K : PortfolioDeleted {portfolioId} (one per portfolio)
K ->> SP : PortfolioDeleted
SP -> OBJ : delete the site pages and snapshots
SP -> CDN : invalidate /{slug}/*
K ->> MS : UserDeleted
MS -> OBJ : delete originals and derivatives of the account
MS -> CDN : invalidate cached media
K ->> AGG : PortfolioDeleted
AGG -> CH : delete raw events of the portfolio\n(aggregated counts hold no personal data)

note over CH
  Every consumer retries until it succeeds.
  The account row stays as a tombstone with
  its identifier until all services confirm.
end note
@enduml
